WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.080
We're standing in front of the building that
houses the Commission on Presidential Debates,

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.780
back in 2000 they said 'hey you gotta be at
15% in five national polls that we pick.'

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:16.080
Gary Johnson and Bill Weld, they did not cut
it with the American public, they're at 8.6-8.4%

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.990
according to real clear politics, why should
they be in?

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:24.130
The polls were not correct, they didn't ask
about him on the first question, I read all

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:29.890
the methodologies, and there, his name was
buried down deep into the questions and also

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:35.750
the CNN / ORC poll that came out, if you look
at every single page from 18-34 year olds

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.960
it was N/A so they didn't get enough statistical
data to even represent it.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.040
Certain polls have under-represented 35 and
under,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.400
other polls have under-represented independents.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:52.640
Independents make up half of the voting population
in the United States and some polls only polled

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:59.040
Democrats and Republicans and they only included
about 15% representation from Independents.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.680
There's a groundswell of opinion in this country
that we need multi-party politics or third

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.790
party politics and it just so happens that,
you know, history has set the table with Johnson/Weld,

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:14.110
it's such a strong ticket that if these guys
can't be the damn-breakers to get us, you

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.440
know, to multi-party politics, nobody's going
to.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.060
But I got to tell you it's the extremists
on both sides that are ruining America.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:27.320
So you see Gary Johnson and Bill Weld as centrists,
you know, because normally the knock on Libertarians

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:32.700
is that, they're these crazy people out there
on the horizon talking about, you know, selling

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.560
crack cocaine in grammar school.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.140
I just, I don't, I see their side of it.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.120
But I'm not gonna agree with any candidate
100%,

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.500
the only person I'm gonna agree with 100% of the time is myself.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:53.280
So, barring that, I align myself to Johnson/Weld
more than any other.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.340
I don't agree with everything Gary Johnson
has to say.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:59.700
But right now he's the only one in the middle,
he's only Libertarian who has any chance of

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.579
getting on the national stage and saying,
like 'Hey, we can agree to disagree.

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:07.500
But the number one priority in America has
to be liberty.'

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.560
What do you like most about Gary Johnson?

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.870
That he's speaking honestly about the issues
I'm concerned about which are the tax code

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:20.560
and how complicated it's become and social
security which needs to be reformed.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.890
I believe he's the best choice for our country.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:27.470
And I want a smaller government, hopefully
want to get some of the troops home,

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:29.040
stop all the stupid wars.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:34.091
You said earlier, you drove all the way from
Boston, that is some kinda commitment, would

00:02:34.091 --> 00:02:36.250
you do that for any other presidential candidate?

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.250
Absolutely not.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.230
I am outraged at the thought of a Clinton
or Trump presidency.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:45.989
I think it's embarrassing, I think it's embarrassing
for America that we are going to have people

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:52.730
that are known crooks and liars speaking for
us and basically being our American icon.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:57.680
Well we're here protesting the decision not
to let Gary debate and obviously we all want

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.760
Gary on that stage with the other two candidates.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.720
And we wouldn't mind seeing Jill up there
too.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.269
Johnson's views align with mine very well.

00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:10.761
Any small L libertarian republican, and I
think that's a huge part of the party, would

00:03:10.761 --> 00:03:12.820
be happy to support him.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:18.160
But I also think that we're teaching our kids
to vote for bad people.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.370
We're telling our children 'the two party
system has nominated these two candidates

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:26.379
and they're your only choice' and everyone
who supports those two candidates I hear them

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:31.220
saying 'yeah I hate my candidate but they're
less of a liar than the other candidate.'

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:35.030
And less of a liar is not a good reason to
vote for someone.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:41.290
He's now on all 50 ballots plus the District
of Columbia, and I think it's imperative for

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:46.640
the American people to understand truly what
their choice is and they do have an alternative

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:49.739
choice to Trump and Hillary.

00:03:49.739 --> 00:03:55.480
Are you a, traditionally are you a Republican,
a Democrat, Libertarian, where do you fall?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:58.980
I've always been a Democrat, and always voted
that way.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.250
What do you think explains his immense popularity
among younger people?

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:07.239
Well, of course, Libertarians were a little
worried with the Bernie phenomenon, that the

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:11.580
milleniums who liked Ron Paul just four and
eight years ago were suddenly going socialist.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:16.499
But, you know, their concern about Hillary
I think is making them look at Gary or Jill

00:04:16.499 --> 00:04:21.180
Stein and seeing his liberal positions on
a lot of social issues, whether it's the drug

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:26.639
war or intervention overseas, regime change,
or privacy, you know, the surveillance state,

00:04:26.639 --> 00:04:32.469
over-criminalization, a host of issues where
Governor Johnson is better than Hillary on.

00:04:32.469 --> 00:04:34.779
I've never done this, we're not activists.

00:04:34.779 --> 00:04:39.159
I've never even put a bumper sticker on my
car, I've never donated to a campaign.

